          "settings": {
            "question": "Licensed Aesthetician:",
            "answer": "<p>The Aeroderm functions as an indispensable asset during deep-pore cleansing and manual extraction pre-conditioning. By pairing its calibrated pneumatic suction with the targeted glass blackhead remover cupping component, the practicing aesthetician can effortlessly pull surface impurities out of the follicular walls. This mechanical approach replaces aggressive physical manual squeezing, protecting the specialist from repetitive wrist strain while offering the client a comfortable, inflammation-free clearing session.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_74hYTC": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Clinical Spa Technician:",
            "answer": "<p>In high-volume clinical rooms, maintaining a strict procedural tempo is critical to daily profitability. The Aeroderm integrates a dual-mode active system featuring independent misting lines and vacuum suction paths that adjust on demand. This permits the technician to transition instantly from active pore purging to refreshing spray misting without power lag, reducing treatment downtime and delivering immediate, repeatable skin calming after intensive resurfacing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_bhzmwM": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Specialized Skincare Consultant:",
            "answer": "<p>For diagnostic consultations and customized facial massage routines, the unit delivers fine-tuned variable intensity adjustments. Utilizing the specialized anti-wrinkle and facial massage glass suction cups, the consultant can perform delicate lymphatic sweeping safely along sensitive dermal pathways. This mechanical stimulation improves localized circulation and product responsiveness, offering visible skin plumping and a premium sensory experience.</p>"
          }
        }
